- Host runtime: `Darwin 25.6.0 arm64`; `go version go1.26.4 darwin/arm64`.
- Linux runtime: Docker daemon `linux/aarch64`; image `golang:1.26` resolves to
  `linux/arm64`; container ran with `--init`, `GOMAXPROCS=2`, Go 1.26.
- Linux evidence applies to that arm64 image/container setup. It is not a claim
  about other Docker init arrangements. An earlier no-init attempt stalled
  during dependency download and was stopped without a test result. A container
  PID 1 that does not reap orphaned killed children can leave a zombie visible
  in the old process group, so the safe result in that setup may remain
  quarantined. Do not treat the `--init` runtime result as evidence for no-init.

