Exit code: 0; `ok github.com/pengjunchen/go-cli/internal/tools 6.617s`.

The finite sshpass escape fixture creates a helper that calls `setsid`, waits
for cancellation of the owned local group, then writes a marker and exits. The
tool returns unknown/pending while that child can still run; its
`ExecutionDone` stays open even after the finite helper exits because local
transport quiescence is not a remote completion receipt. The test waits for
the finite helper to exit and verifies its process group disappears, so it
does not leave a long-lived child.

