## Output and containment boundaries

The retained stdout+stderr source bytes share the configured cap. StreamingBash
preserves LF, CRLF, and EOF-tail source bytes. Display framing may add one
synthetic separator newline and a fixed truncation marker outside that source
budget. The local process metadata field `containment_scope=process_group`
describes only the group created for that invocation; it is not general process
tree or sandbox containment. A child that deliberately calls `setsid` or
`setpgid` and redirects/closes inherited pipes is outside the Unix process-group
guarantee and may be unobservable. Password-mode sshpass launches its SSH child
in a new session; therefore local group stop cannot prove that the local SSH
transport tree or remote command stopped. Remote cancellation/transport
ambiguity remains unknown and pending without a remote receipt.
